    "rule": "Per basin: residual R contains conditional context info ONLY IF BOTH (i) the PersA+R (=TSAR) increment paired-CI excludes 0 AND (ii) within matched-DHW bins R shows a stable positive association with future severe outcome. Otherwise not proven.",
    "text": "The TSAR residual R provides conditional context information beyond PersA_DHW in the two transfer target basins gbr and CARIB: there BOTH (i) the PersA+R (=TSAR) increment paired-CI excludes 0 (GBR ΔROC +0.0006 [+0.0002,+0.0014], ΔPR +0.063 [+0.015,+0.127]; CARIB ΔROC +0.0029 [+0.0013,+0.0046], ΔPR +0.084 [+0.057,+0.114]) and (ii) within matched-DHW (0.05) bins R remains positively associated with future severe outcome (Spearman rho CI excluding 0; severe-rate rises with R within fixed DHW, e.g. CARIB bin[0.75,0.80): severe-rate 0.13 (R-Q1) -> 0.67 (R-Q3)). R is therefore not merely re-encoding DHW in these basins. In the source basin SCS the residual adds no marginal increment (TSAR≈PersA by the conservative source-anchor design; ΔROC -0.001, CI includes 0), so conditional-residual info is not established there and is not claimed. Methodological caveat: the within-DHW Spearman association alone is positive in all basins (R encodes the 'is DHW rising?' context), so the CI-supported marginal increment is the discriminating evidence for where R adds transferable value."
